# Third-party content

The work original to this repository is MIT licensed; see LICENSE. Part of
`account/claude/` is third-party or derived from third-party work, and those files
carry the terms below rather than the MIT licence.

The account layer is generated by `install/Export-Account.ps1` from a workstation's
`~/.claude/` tree, so these directories arrived there by installation rather than by
being authored here. They are redistributed so a second machine comes up configured
the same way.

That is also why this notice names directories and never counts them. The exporter
rewrites the tree on every run, so a file count taken here measures a file nobody in
this repository owns, goes stale the moment somebody installs a skill, and falsifies
a licence attribution with nothing reporting the change. `CONTRIBUTING.md` states the
general rule. Read each directory named below as covering everything inside it, and
take the count from `git ls-files` when a count is what you need.

## Security skill knowledge bases

`account/claude/skills/owasp-agentic/`, `owasp-cicd/`, `owasp-infrastructure/`,
`owasp-llm/`, `owasp-mcp/`, `owasp-top-10/` and `secure-by-design/`.

Every tree named above comes from `microsoft/hve-core`, which each `SKILL.md` names in
its description. They were installed from there rather than derived from the primary
sources directly, and each tree records its own upstream in a `content_based_on`
frontmatter field.

The `owasp-*` trees named above carry `license: CC-BY-SA-4.0` and name the OWASP
Foundation as author. Content derived from works by the OWASP Foundation, licensed
under CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/). ShareAlike
applies: adaptations of this material distributed onward must carry the same licence.

`secure-by-design/` carries `license: OGL-UK-3.0 AND CC-BY-4.0`. Content derived from
works by the UK Government Security Group (Crown Copyright) licensed under the Open
Government Licence v3.0
(https://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/doc/open-government-licence/version/3/), and by
the Australian Signals Directorate / ACSC (© Commonwealth of Australia) licensed under
CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).

Licence marking inside these trees is uneven, which this notice exists to cover. Each
tree's `SKILL.md` carries the SPDX `license:` field. The reference files under
`owasp-cicd/`, `owasp-infrastructure/` and `owasp-mcp/` carry no marker of their own.
Read the attribution here as applying to every file in the trees named above.

